<div class="card"><h2>Why Americans Choose China for Treatment</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Direct flights:</strong> 12–14 hours non-stop from LAX, SFO, NYC, Chicago, Seattle to Beijing, Shanghai, Guangzhou.</li><li><strong>English-speaking doctors:</strong> All recommended hospitals have international departments with fluent English staff; many surgeons trained in the US.</li><li><strong>JCI accreditation:</strong> Top Chinese hospitals meet the same standards as leading US academic centers.</li><li><strong>Short scheduling:</strong> Elective procedures are often scheduled within 2–4 weeks of consultation — we confirm exact timing with the hospital for your case.</li><li><strong>L visa:</strong> US citizens qualify for a 10-year multiple-entry L visa; hospitals provide invitation letters to support your application.</li></ul></div>

<div class="card"><h2>How We Help US Patients</h2><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Tell us your condition, city preference, and budget — free, no commitment.</p><p><strong>Step 2:</strong> We match you with 2-3 hospitals and compare costs vs US prices, with transport guidance.</p><p><strong>Step 3:</strong> We coordinate records, appointments, and airport pickup. You fly from the US — we handle the rest.</p><p><strong>Cost:</strong> From $49 (hospital shortlist) to $399 (full journey management), with $149 verification in between. No hidden fees, no hospital commissions. <a href="pricing.html">See pricing →</a></p></div>

